WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:14.988
SHOW ONLY THE SA LAYER
In the Explorer, ⊞ on SA scopes every diagram to the system-analysis package. The chip above the canvas says what is shown.

2
00:00:14.988 --> 00:00:27.264
GENERAL VIEW
Definitions and usages as boxes, read left to right. At SA the system is one part, system, with functions allocated to it and requirements it satisfies.

3
00:00:27.264 --> 00:00:37.388
READ ONE ELEMENT
Select a box: Properties shows what it is. Selection zooms to it. system is the twelve-drone swarm as one black box.

4
00:00:37.388 --> 00:00:47.236
TREE VIEW
What SA contains, one branch at a time. +N on a box opens what it owns — here SwarmMember, with its two state machines.

5
00:00:47.236 --> 00:00:57.838
INTERCONNECTION VIEW
The system and its actors, with ports on their edges. Each line is a connection: tasking, supervision, recall, reports.

6
00:00:57.838 --> 00:01:13.905
ACTION VIEW
The 26 functions of the system and its actors: a set allocated to owners, not a sequence. The 13 lines are flows, labelled with what they carry: a detection report goes to acknowledgement, a receipt comes back.

7
00:01:13.905 --> 00:01:26.409
STATE VIEW
Each drone has two state machines: where it is in its sortie, and its operating condition. The fleet has mesh modes. Arrows are transitions: trigger / effect.

8
00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:39.020
ADD A STATE BACK
Before recording we deleted Readmitted from SwarmMemberModes. Now we add it back. A new element goes under the selection, so first open SA › SwarmMember.

9
00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:45.546
SELECT WHERE IT GOES
Select the state machine SwarmMemberModes in the Explorer.

10
00:01:45.546 --> 00:01:57.680
PLACE A STATE
Pick State in the palette, then click empty canvas. The new state is created inside SwarmMemberModes; until it has a transition it stands on its own.

11
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:04.599
NAME IT
Type the name in Properties.

12
00:02:04.599 --> 00:02:14.257
CONNECT IT
Pick Transition, click the source state, then the target: Quarantined → Readmitted. The new transition is selected.

13
00:02:14.257 --> 00:02:25.481
GIVE IT A TRIGGER AND AN EFFECT
In Properties: the trigger readmissionPassed, the effect rejoinAfterCheck. The line is labelled trigger / effect.

14
00:02:25.481 --> 00:02:34.399
AND ONWARD
Once checked, a readmitted drone returns to Nominal: Readmitted → Nominal.

15
00:02:34.399 --> 00:02:45.325
THE RESULT
Readmitted is back between Quarantined and Nominal, as before we deleted it. Edits stay in this browser until you save or export them.

16
00:02:45.325 --> 00:02:56.053
REQUIREMENT VIEW
Requirements and what satisfies each one. SwarmMember satisfies most of SA's; functions such as admitMember satisfy the rest.

17
00:02:56.053 --> 00:03:05.176
CASE VIEW
The eleven use cases, from WatchTheTaskedArea to SwarmSelfCoordination, each with the system as its subject.
